  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{log}_{2}\\,(x+{b}^{2}), & x\\le 3 \\\\ x-1, & x>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nis continuous at  $x=3,$  find the possible values of $b.$\n\nArranged in **ascending order**,\n\n$b=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,b=$\n\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "At $x=3,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{log}_{2}\\,(x+{b}^{2})={log}_{2}\\,(3+{b}^{2}),\n$$\n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}(x-1)=3-1=2.\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=3,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}g(x) \\\\ {log}_{2}\\,(3+{b}^{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3+{b}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ 3+{b}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {b}^{2} & =1 \\\\ b & =-1,\\,1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function is continuous at $x=3$ for the values\n\n$$\nb=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,b=1.\n$$",
